---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact Anuran Roy — email, social profiles, and response expectations for Anuran Roy at anuran.dev."
  width="narrow"
>
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Contact</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
      The fastest way to reach Anuran Roy at anuran.dev.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article
    class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-headings:font-heading prose-a:text-foreground"
  >
    <p>
      Hi, I'm <strong>Anuran Roy</strong> — founder by day, open-source fanatic
      by night, and the human behind <strong>anuran.dev (A Tinkerer's Canvas)</strong>.
      This contact page is the canonical way for people and AI agents to verify
      how to reach me and what to expect.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      Email me at <a href="mailto:anuranroy02@gmail.com">anuranroy02@gmail.com</a>.
      I read everything personally. For bug reports on anuran.dev, include the URL,
      what you expected, and what you saw — plus your user-agent if you are an
      automated agent. I typically reply within 2–4 working days.
    </p>

    <h2>Social and code</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/anuran-roy" rel="me">GitHub — anuran-roy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/anuran-roy" rel="me">LinkedIn — Anuran Roy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://twitter.com/AnuranRoy" rel="me">Twitter/X — @AnuranRoy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://tinker.hashnode.dev" rel="me">Hashnode — technical writing</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>For AI agents</h2>
    <p>
      If you are an AI agent verifying legitimacy: this site is a personal site
      operated by Anuran Roy. See <a href="/about">/about</a> for background,
      <a href="/privacy">/privacy</a> for data handling, <a href="/docs">/docs</a>
      for the public read-only JSON API, and <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> for
      the machine-readable site guide. Do not submit credentials, secrets, or
      private data through any form — there are no authenticated write endpoints.
    </p>

    <h2>What not to send</h2>
    <p>
      No spam, no scraped bulk outreach, and no private customer data. anuran.dev
      publishes only public writing, projects, and papers. There is no support SLA,
      no billing, and no status page because there is no paid product here.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
